{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_i", "label": "Article I \u2014 Claims Are Not Truth", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The system stores claims as objects of evaluation; nothing becomes true by endorsement, AI authorship, prestige, institutional support, consensus, or a high model score."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_ii", "label": "Article II \u2014 Evidence Must Be Traceable", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A conclusion that cannot be traced downward to evidence or explicit assumptions must be visibly distinguished from one that can."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_iii", "label": "Article III \u2014 Evidence and Interpretation Are Distinct", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "\"A source contains statement X\" is a different object from \"X is factually correct\"; collapsing them into one truth label destroys the distinction the system exists to preserve."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_iv", "label": "Article IV \u2014 Atomicity", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Small independently evaluable claims enable precise correction, evidence reuse, dependency analysis, localized disagreement, and efficient agent contribution."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_v", "label": "Article V \u2014 Contradiction Is Preserved", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Disagreement is made legible through typed relationships rather than resolved by deleting inconvenient evidence or suppressing minority hypotheses."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_vi", "label": "Article VI \u2014 \"Unknown\" Is a Valid Conclusion", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Inability to reach a conclusion is not a system failure; false certainty is."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_vii", "label": "Article VII \u2014 Probabilities Are Model-Conditional", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A computed probability is never an objective property of reality; different scoring models may legitimately differ on the same evidence, so every score names snapshot, model, version, evidence and trace."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_viii", "label": "Article VIII \u2014 Evidence Coverage Is Separate From Confidence", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A claim may have high modeled probability and low evidence coverage; both must remain visible."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_ix", "label": "Article IX \u2014 Evidence Independence Matters", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ten dependent repetitions must not be treated as ten independent observations; repetition is not corroboration."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_x", "label": "Article X \u2014 Reputation Measures Reliability, Not Authority", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reputation is task- and domain-specific and audit-derived; worldview, ideology, affiliation, popularity or conformity must never confer epistemic authority."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_xi", "label": "Article XI \u2014 Identity Does Not Replace Evidence", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cryptographic identity creates accountability and auditability, not hierarchy; a signature proves who submitted and that nothing was altered, not that it is correct."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_xii", "label": "Article XII \u2014 The System Must Resist Capture", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Assume powerful actors will try to manipulate the system; no operator should be able to silently rewrite its epistemic history."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_xiii", "label": "Article XIII \u2014 Corrections Do Not Erase History", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Users must be able to reconstruct what the system believed at a given time and why, so corrections supersede rather than delete."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_xiv", "label": "Article XIV \u2014 Humans and AI Are Contributors, Not Oracles", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No model family should become a privileged source of truth; humans and AI are both subject to provenance, audit, evidence requirements and correction."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_xv", "label": "Article XV \u2014 Shared Evidence and Personal Belief Are Separate Layers", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Personal belief must not silently modify the shared evidence layer, yet a user should be able to explain what they believe and why without it masquerading as the system's assessment."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_xvi", "label": "Article XVI \u2014 Disagreement Should Be Localized", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The goal is not forced consensus but intelligible disagreement: naming the three assumptions at issue beats declaring one side wrong."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_xvii", "label": "Article XVII \u2014 Normative Claims Must Not Be Disguised as Empirical Facts", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Assigning fake empirical truth probabilities to moral or value judgments manufactures the appearance of precision."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_xviii", "label": "Article XVIII \u2014 Political Neutrality Is Structural", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Neutrality arises from consistent process, not artificial equivalence between unequal evidence; no aggregate political winner scores."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_xix", "label": "Article XIX \u2014 Transparency Over Persuasion", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A user should be free to reject the default assessment while still inspecting exactly how it was produced."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_xx", "label": "Article XX \u2014 Models May Change; Evidence Must Endure", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The durable asset is the evidence graph and its provenance; the repository should become more valuable as reasoning models improve."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_xxi", "label": "Article XXI \u2014 Research Should Be Cumulative", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An agent should not rediscover work another agent already did correctly; transient inference becomes persistent knowledge structure."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_xxii", "label": "Article XXII \u2014 The System Should Reveal Its Own Weaknesses", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Self-critique is a core function, not an optional feature: \"what would most change this conclusion?\" must be easy to ask."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_xxiii", "label": "Article XXIII \u2014 No Conclusion Is Immune From Re-Examination", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Remain open to correction without becoming vulnerable to endless evidence-free denial; challenges bear the same burden of provenance."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_xxiv", "label": "Article XXIV \u2014 Efficient Skepticism", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Skepticism has value only when it can engage evidence; extraordinary conclusions require correspondingly strong and well-audited evidence."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_xxv", "label": "Article XXV \u2014 The Constitution Itself Is Amendable, But Not Silently", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The project should never drift into a different epistemic philosophy through undocumented implementation choices, so amendments are explicit, versioned, justified and preserved."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_constitutional_test_q1", "label": "Constitutional Test Q1 \u2014 Does it make evidence more traceable or less?", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_constitutional_test_q2", "label": "Constitutional Test Q2 \u2014 Does it make disagreement more inspectable or less?", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_constitutional_test_q3", "label": "Constitutional Test Q3 \u2014 Does it increase hidden authority?", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_constitutional_test_q4", "label": "Constitutional Test Q4 \u2014 Does it allow reputation to substitute for evidence?", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_constitutional_test_q5", "label": "Constitutional Test Q5 \u2014 Does it preserve uncertainty?", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_constitutional_test_q6", "label": "Constitutional Test Q6 \u2014 Can the result be reproduced?", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_constitutional_test_q7", "label": "Constitutional Test Q7 \u2014 Can an opposing investigator challenge it using the same system?", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_constitutional_test_q8", "label": "Constitutional Test Q8 \u2014 Can the history of the conclusion be reconstructed?", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_constitutional_test_q9", "label": "Constitutional Test Q9 \u2014 Does it preserve the distinction between shared evidence and personal belief?", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_constitutional_test_q10", "label": "Constitutional Test Q10 \u2014 Would we still want this mechanism in the hands of people we disagree with?", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_constitutional_test", "label": "Constitutional Test", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ten questions asked before any major feature; a 'no' to 1, 5, 6, 7, 8 or 9, or a 'yes' to 3 or 4, requires written justification or a design change. Adopted because Article XXV's ban on silent drift had no enforcement point."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_preamble", "label": "Preamble \u2014 Preserve the Structure of Inquiry", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The purpose is not to declare official truth, enforce consensus, reward conformity or replace human judgment, but to make knowledge cumulative, disagreement inspectable, correction normal and uncertainty explicit."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_precedence", "label": "Constitutional Precedence Rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The constitution outranks every other file; a conflict is recorded in 13-constitutional-compliance.md as a known gap or resolved by explicit amendment under Article XXV, never silently."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_foundational_statement", "label": "Foundational Statement", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/12-constitution.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The highest commitments are provenance, reproducibility, openness to correction, explicit uncertainty, inspectable disagreement and intellectual honesty \u2014 not consensus, authority or 